module gunbc.namespace_wave_admission

import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import std.types { String, List }
import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung_drop {
  GuaranteeStall,
  Mitigatable,
  MechanicallyPreventable,
  AwaitsOneGrounding,
  BoundedPopulation,
}

// WHY THIS CARRIER EXISTS BESIDE THE WALL RATHER THAN INSIDE THE PLAN IT ENFORCES. The
// enforcement mechanism was dispatched OUTSIDE the import/namespace program deliberately --
// the program's own owning session declined ownership of it on the ground that a program
// parented over its enforcement grades its own homework -- so what counts as ADMISSIBLE is
// homed here, and what the deltas MEAN over the import population stays with that program.

data namespace_wave_admission_note: String = "THE REQUIRED WAVE-ADMISSION WALL over closure, subject-membership and occurrence-binding deltas: gunbc.compiler_frontend_program_interlock milestone NamespaceWaveAdmissionEnrolled.\n\nWHAT IT ANSWERS. For one change, at merge-base grain: which modules entered or left each module's subject, what each module's transitive closure gained or lost, and whether any spelling already authored on both sides changed WHICH DECLARATIONS IT ADMITS. Every motion is classified into NamespaceDeltaDisposition and the run is ADMITTED only when the UNADJUDICATED set is empty -- never when the delta is empty, which is the one-word difference the ruling states explicitly and the weaker spelling of which would refuse the cut itself and then be repaired by weakening the wall.\n\nWHERE IT RUNS. As the namespace-wave-admission phase of claim_executor --required-ci, in the witnesses lane, consuming the index the parse phase built. It acquires no second corpus: the base index is the head index with the diff applied in reverse at FILE grain, so only the files a change touched are parsed again, from their base blobs, while closure and binding are recomputed over both whole graphs -- a module whose own text did not move can still have its subject moved by one that did.\n\nTHE CHANGE CLASS IS DERIVED, NOT DECLARED. NamespaceChangeClass splits preparatory work from work that alters membership or binding. Nothing asks an author which they wrote: the delta is measured and the answer falls out, so PreparatoryNoSemanticMotion is a property of a diff rather than a claim in a pull-request body. Construction over validation.\n\nTWO NON-VERDICTS ARE REPORTED UNDER THEIR OWN NAMES AND ONLY ONE PASSES. A push whose baseline IS its own head -- main after a squash merge -- has no diff to adjudicate, and that is NoSubject: nothing was compared and nothing is admitted. A baseline that does not resolve is NotEvaluated, which the ruling puts on the refusing side, because I could not see what changed and nothing changed are different states with different remedies and the second is the empty-observation narrow.\n\nA STALE ADMISSION REFUSES TOO. A transition-admission row matching no delta is a permission standing over nothing; leaving it would let the roster stop being a fact about the corpus and become a list nobody pruned."

// WHY THE GRAIN IS AUTHORED CONTAINMENT IDENTITY AND NOT OCCURRENCE IDENTITY, which is a CLOSED
// RESULT rather than a shortcut.
//
// v2.workflow.legacy_binding_delta states it for its own subject and the argument transfers
// unchanged: std.occurrence_identity's scope law forbids filename, SourceSpan, authored name,
// structural Node equality and content hash as identity inputs, and an OccurrenceId is a monotone
// counter consumed in walk order, so it ENCODES POSITION and shifts under any edit above it. A
// cross-compile correspondence is therefore something a TRANSFORMATION EMITS -- a function knows
// which output came from which input -- and between a merge base and a pull-request head there is
// no transformation to emit one. So an occurrence-grain delta between two arbitrary trees is not a
// better key waiting to be found; it is unavailable by construction.
//
// WHAT THE WALL USES INSTEAD is the identity legacy_binding_observation legacy_subject_identity
// already folds for its own subjects, read at the grain a cross-tree join can carry: module path,
// enclosing declaration, and the LEAF SEGMENT of the reference rather than its whole spelling. A
// row's VALUE is the SET of declaring identities that leaf admits, never a winner -- so a local
// declaration arriving beside an imported one WIDENS the set to two and reports NewAmbiguity,
// rather than silently picking the nearer one, which is the mechanism the namespace authority
// exists to delete.
//
// THE LEAF RATHER THAN THE SPELLING IS AN INVARIANT OF THE OPERATION THE CUT PERFORMS, NOT A LUCKY
// FIXTURE. A requalification wave prepends the declarer's path to a reference and leaves the
// declarer fixed, so it changes the authored SPELLING and leaves the last segment unchanged BY
// CONSTRUCTION -- the key does not merely happen to survive the cut, it is invariant under exactly
// the transformation the cut applies. The reduction is not coined here either: v1.05_emit_rust
// rust_fn_sig_leaf_name_dotted_note names qualified_last_segment as THE single authority for taking
// an authored spelling to its last segment, and records a real defect from a site that skipped it
// and emitted dots into Rust output. Stated as an invariant rather than as a finding because a
// finding invites re-litigation and an invariant does not (measured against the carriers by
// snappy-dove-250, 2026-08-26). Keyed on the whole spelling instead, requalifying a reference reads
// as NewUnresolvedness, and the wall would refuse the only program it exists to admit -- which is
// how this was found, by a fixture going red rather than by review.
//
// THE CONVERSE IS THE WALL WORKING AND IS NOT TO BE SOFTENED. If a cut ever repoints a reference to
// a DIFFERENT declaration whose leaf differs, the key moves and the wall refuses. The owning
// program has bound itself to splitting that out rather than asking for tolerance: a wave that both
// requalifies and moves a symbol is two change classes in one diff, and TargetChanged firing on it
// is the wall reporting a mis-shaped wave. No per-row exemption, threshold or allowance is admitted
// for that case -- a confidence threshold selecting a softer arm is the smuggled heuristic DESIGN
// rules out, and it would convert the one signal that catches a mis-shaped wave into silence.
//
// THE CEILING, STATED SO IT IS NOT MISREAD AS COVERAGE: two occurrences of one spelling inside one
// declaration share a row, so WHICH occurrence took which member of the set is not observable here.
// ANYONE READING THE MILESTONE AS COVERING OCCURRENCE GRAIN WILL BE READING MORE THAN EXISTS, and
// that sentence is carried here rather than only in a pull-request body because a body is not an
// authority and the overclaim it prevents is the kind that recurs. The milestone
// NamespaceWaveAdmissionEnrolled delivers two adjudicated walls -- subject membership and binding
// at authored containment grain -- a MEASURED closure blast radius attributed to its generators,
// and this declared stall. It does not deliver a third wall over closure, and it does not deliver
// occurrence grain.
//
// NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a projector-emitted correspondence (legacy_binding_delta
// ProjectionProvenanceEntry) reaching a base/head pair, at which point the row key descends to the
// occurrence and this note is deleted rather than amended.

// WHY THE BINDING CHANNEL IS NOT THE IMPORT CHANNEL, which is the load-bearing design choice.
//
// A wall reading bindings only through import members would observe the import-name universe being
// deleted and then see NOTHING AT ALL -- blind on precisely the change it gates, in the first wave
// it exists to govern. So the channel is every authored NAME OCCURRENCE in a module's own parsed
// tree, resolved independently: a dotted spelling by its longest module prefix, a bare spelling
// against the module's own declarations and its import claims, following a re-export chain to the
// module that actually DECLARES the name. It survives the cut because it never depended on the
// construct being cut, and the FUNCTION is the same on both sides, so a base measured before a cut
// and a head measured after it are measured by one instrument.
//
// IT IS PARSE-THEN-DERIVE AND NOT A TEXT SCANNER. DESIGN's namespace-cut correction ruled the
// raw-text scanner family -- referenced_module_paths_in_text and kin -- a heuristic that cannot
// distinguish a reference from prose, with the in-tree receipt of the English word edge binding to
// fn edge. This reads the Node tree. What it does NOT do is resolve: a parameter name, a field name
// and a let binder land in the same set as a genuine reference, because telling them apart is the
// resolver's job. That over-collection is SYMMETRIC across two trees, which is the only property
// the delta needs -- a spelling denoting nothing on both sides contributes no row.
//
// WHERE THAT IS CONSERVATIVE AND IN WHICH DIRECTION, because an approximation whose direction is
// unstated is a hole. On the BINDING channel it can only produce rows about spellings that are not
// references, and such a row is a delta only if its candidate set actually moved -- so the
// direction is toward refusing, never toward admitting. On the MEMBERSHIP-SUPPORT question -- does
// any name in this module reach into the target -- it is toward admitting, and that is deliberate:
// refusing an added dependency because the reader could not see the reference would make ordinary
// work an adjudication, and a wall paid for in false refusals is a wall that gets weakened.

// WHAT THE WALL DOES WITH CLOSURE, AND THE ARM IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT AUTHOR.
//
// Closure is a pure function of membership, so the closure moved and no membership moved is not a
// state any fixture can author. An arm for it would be permanently green by construction -- the
// decoration DESIGN 4b calls worse than absent, because it gets cited as coverage. Closure is
// therefore MEASURED and ATTRIBUTED rather than separately adjudicated: every moved closure row is
// grouped under the membership delta that generates it, and each delta carries the number of
// modules whose subject it moves, so a refusal names its blast radius. The adjudication happens at
// the generators, which is where the decision is; adjudicating the consequence as well would be a
// second representation of one fact.
//
// SO THE THREE DELTAS THE MILESTONE NAMES ARE NOT THREE WALLS. Two are adjudicated and the third is
// the derived consequence of one of them, reported beside it. Saying so here is the difference
// between a scope statement and an inflated one.

// THE TRANSITION-ADMISSION ROSTER IS EMPTY AT LANDING, AND THAT IS THE CORRECT STATE: no wave has
// run, so no transition has been authorised. A row names one exact subject under one exact
// disposition, and a row matching no delta refuses as stale, so the roster can only shrink toward
// its subject.
//
// WHAT THE FIRST WAVE WILL NEED, RECORDED NOW AND NOT BUILT NOW. The import/namespace program's
// owning session measured the expected magnitude against the import-strip receipts: THOUSANDS of
// transitions, dominated by one class. That figure is STALE AS A POPULATION -- the same anchor
// recipe re-run on 2026-08-26 returns a different corpus hash than the receipts record, so the
// receipts describe no current tree -- and it is quoted here ONLY as an order of magnitude, which
// is the part that decides a design question. A per-row roster at that scale is unreviewable, and
// an unreviewable roster is rubber-stamped, which converts this wall into a formality.
//
// SO A CLASS ADMISSION MUST BE BOUNDED BY ENUMERATED IDENTITY AND NEVER BY PREDICATE. These exact
// bindings, taken from the pre-deletion baseline observation, become unresolved is admissible;
// unresolvedness is expected during the wave is not, because it admits everything and zeroes the
// wall's deficit frequency by construction -- the absorbing fallback wearing the wave's clothes.
// The distinction is the whole difference between a wall that survives its own transition and one
// that is switched off for its duration.
//
// THE POPULATION ARRIVES ONE GRAIN DOWN FROM THIS WALL'S ROWS, AND THE PROJECTION IS THE RECEIVING
// END'S JOB. Measured on the carrier rather than assumed: std.legacy_binding_observation
// LegacyBindingObservationRow carries exactly two fields, an occurrence identity and an outcome --
// no module, no enclosing declaration, no leaf. So a class admission enumerated from the baseline
// observation cannot hand this wall its key directly. The route down is the leaf from the validated
// occurrence transport's index entries, whose OccurrenceProjection authored_name is the authored
// spelling; the enclosing declaration from the occurrence containment path's ancestors joined
// against that transport's declarations; and the module from the containment root.
//
// ONE TRAP ON THAT ROUTE, NAMED BECAUSE IT FAILS SILENTLY. authored_name CARRIES DOTS --
// v1.02_parse populates it from the raw node name and every consumption site applies
// qualified_last_segment to reduce it. Keying on authored_name raw reproduces exactly the spelling
// hazard the grain note above rejects, and reproduces it INVISIBLY, because on an unqualified
// reference the spelling and the leaf are identical and every naturally-written test passes. The
// reduction is not optional and is not this module's to re-coin.
//
// WHY THE COARSE CARRIER IS NOT AUTHORED HERE. It would be a mechanism with no consumer until a
// wave needs it, and a new artifact with no final consumer is the experimental residue DESIGN 6
// names. What is fixed today is the CONSTRAINT on its shape, not the shape itself; the population
// it enumerates comes from the milestone NamespaceBaselineObservationComplete, and where that
// baseline is unavailable for the base being gated, the honest disposition is NotEvaluated refusing
// rather than a predicate substituted for a missing enumeration.

// THE RUNG, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT REACH. The class is a namespace change merging with its
// closure, membership or binding motion unexamined. It was OUTSIDE THE LADDER -- not
// mitigatable, because nothing could be attempted -- and it is now mechanically preventable:
// a required phase, armed on every push and pull request, whose RED is authorable at the
// FIXTURE boundary and is authored there. It is not structurally guaranteed and this row does
// not claim it: the motion stays perfectly writable and safety depends on the phase executing.

// WHY THE CLOSURE CLAUSE IS ABSENT ON A BINDING ROW RATHER THAN ZERO.
//
// The paragraph above states that closure is a pure function of MEMBERSHIP, so a moved closure row
// groups under the membership delta generating it. The consequence for the carrier is that only a
// membership row can answer the closure question at all, and a binding row is not a row whose
// closure motion is zero -- it is a row that was never asked.
//
// Those two states shared one spelling until the field became optional. A binding delta was
// constructed with a literal zero and the renderer appended the same bracketed clause to every
// row, so an unasked question and a measured zero were byte-identical in the output. That is the
// shape DESIGN 5 forbids: the run emitted a measurement where it had performed none, and the zero
// was available to be read as evidence that a rebinding was contained. The field now carries the
// absence, and the renderer omits the clause rather than rendering a number for it.
//
// SO THE RULE A READER NEEDS: the presence of the clause is what says the question was asked. Its
// absence on a binding row is the honest answer, and no zero should be inferred from it.
//
// THE GUARANTEE THIS REACHES, STATED HONESTLY: mechanically preventable, not structural. The
// invalid state is narrower than it was -- a binding site can no longer default into a measured
// zero, because the not-asked case has its own constructor -- but writing a measured zero at a
// binding site remains authorable. It becomes unwritable when the radius moves onto the membership
// subject itself, which the delta identity cannot carry today: DeltaSubject is the ordered identity
// a transition admission matches against, and a measurement inside an identity would make one
// subject compare unequal to itself across two runs.

data namespace_wave_admission_occurrence_grain_stall: GuaranteeStall = GuaranteeStall {
  subject: "v1_compiler.namespace_wave_admission -- WHICH occurrence of a spelling took which member of its declaring-candidate set, where one declaration carries two occurrences of one spelling",
  current: Mitigatable,
  ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
  blocker: AwaitsOneGrounding {
    grounding: "no transformation emits a correspondence between a merge base and a pull-request head, and v2.workflow.legacy_binding_delta rules that without one there is no admissible cross-compile occurrence key at all -- an OccurrenceId encodes walk position and shifts under any edit above it, so this is a closed result rather than a missing implementation",
  },
  population: BoundedPopulation {
    members: [
      "a spelling shadowed by a let declaration inside the declaration that also reaches it from an outer scope",
      "a spelling shadowed by a lambda or match-arm binder inside the declaration that also reaches it from an outer scope",
      "two references to one leaf inside one declaration where only one of them is requalified",
    ],
  },
  next_rung_trigger: "A projector-emitted correspondence between the two trees being compared -- v2.workflow.legacy_binding_delta ProjectionProvenanceEntry, whose ProjectedFromSource arm relates one target occurrence to its source. The wall's row key descends from the leaf to the occurrence the moment a base/head pair carries one, and the union taken in binding_rows deletes with it. What does NOT close this is a finer key invented here: the scope law rules out every property computable from a finished tree in isolation, so an occurrence key that is not emitted by a transformation is not a stronger key, it is a wrong one."
}

